-- title:
--   Geometric generic fibre model of X₁(Mp) with chart pin
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M\ge 5$ with $p\nmid M$, a characteristic-zero field $L$ that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $p$ together with a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta\in L$, and the intermediate field $K$ of $L((q))/L$ equal to `laurentBaseChange L (x1FunctionField (M * p))`, the $L$-subfield of $L((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion field of $X_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ lies in its image, with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with $A\to L\to K$, and let $j\in K$, $j\ne 0$, have $q$-expansion the coefficientwise image of `jq`; fix compatible embeddings $A\to\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, $L\to\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. The assertion is the existence of: a `CurveModel` $M_\eta$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the field `x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)` $=$ `laurentBaseChange` $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the $q$-expansion field of $X_1(Mp)$ — that is, an integral scheme $M_\eta.C$, proper and smooth of relative dimension $1$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, with a ring isomorphism of that field onto its function field compatible with the structure map, a bijection of its closed points onto the places of the field over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ matching stalks with valuation subrings, and with every finite set of points contained in an affine open — together with a morphism $e_\eta$ from $M_\eta.C$ to the pullback of [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252) along $\operatorname{Spec}\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\to\operatorname{Spec}A$, a proof that $e_\eta$ is an isomorphism, and a proof that the open subscheme of $M_\eta.C$ obtained by pulling back the open image of the finite chart [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.ιFin A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L231) along $e_\eta$ followed by the first projection is non-empty, such that: (1) $e_\eta$ followed by the second projection equals $M_\eta.\mathrm{toBase}$; (2) (chart pin) for every $a$ in the $A$-subalgebra `chartAlgFin A K j` of $K$, transporting $a$ through the global sections of the finite chart, along $e_\eta$ followed by the first projection, taking the germ at the generic point and pulling back by the function-field identification of $M_\eta$ yields the element of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ equal to `coeffMap` of $A\to L\to\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ applied to the Laurent series of $a$; and (3) (Galois compatibility) for every $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra automorphism $g$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ fixing the image of $L$ pointwise and any two sections $x,x'$ of $M_\eta.\mathrm{toBase}$ such that $x'$ followed by $e_\eta$ and the first projection equals $\operatorname{Spec}(g)$ followed by $x$ followed by $e_\eta$ and the first projection, the place attached to $x'$ is the image of the place attached to $x$ under the action of the semilinear automorphism `arithmeticGalois` of $g$, which acts on $q$-expansions coefficientwise.
--
--   This provides the geometric generic fibre data — smooth proper $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-model, comparison isomorphism with the base change of the two-chart integral model over the ramified base, the pinning of the finite chart to $q$-expansions, and compatibility of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points with the arithmetic Galois action on places — for the modular curve $X_1(Mp)$. Its conclusion clauses are exactly the inputs required by the statement on relative sub-Picard representability and Abel–Jacobi points for $X_1(Mp)$ which cites it.
